<title>USA: Sequoia Systems raises share buyback.</title>
<headline>Sequoia Systems raises share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sequoia Systems, which is changing its name to Texas Micro Inc, said on Thursday that it has authorized an increase in its stock repurchase plan by 500,000 shares to 2.5 million.</p>
<p>Effective Thursday, April 24, 1997, Texas Micro will begin trading on the NASDAQ under the stock symbol &quot;TEXM,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>Since the announcement of the repurchase program on September 10, 1996, the company has repurchased 2.2 million shares, the company said.</p>
<p>Texas Micro will report third quarter 1997 results on Wednesday, April 23, 1997.</p>
